6. THE ELECTRICAL ACCEPTANCE ON C-DEV REV 1 (record l9t5 out 5 for the case figures; the makers' sheets read here)
   labels: PRINTED a maker's limit; TYPICAL a maker's typical figure; DECLARED a generator's or a record's declaration; MODEL this record's or another
   record's arithmetic; ASSUMPTION a figure no held document gives; SESSION a choice this record takes
   BOARD A'S HALF (U601, its network, its enable, the device rail's stage)
   (1) U7, the device rail, on the case: 6.0359 A (MODEL: every load at constant power at 4.9019 V, the loads at rv-pwr's HIGH) against its
       average loop's least 7.0957 A (PRINTED VSNS 43 mV, LM5176 SNVSAI1D p.7; R43 6 mOhm at +1 %, DECLARED): margin +1.0598 A: HOLDS
       (before: 7.4717 A, -0.3760 A); the loop's highest 9.5960 A stays under J_5V_DEV's VH 10 A (PRINTED): U7, R43 and its lead unchanged;
       with the draft U7's case no longer carries the supervisors at all, whatever they draw
       LABELLED SCENARIO, not the case (stream s99's declared tier: the wall host port at U32's nominal limit 0.9142 A as well; the case carries
       no wall port load): 6.9501 A against 7.0957 A, +0.1456 A; against the note's conditional 7.056897 A (an assumed 50 K at the shunt), +0.1068 A
   (2) U601 on the case: the three LDOs' own current 1.3800 A = 3 x (0.400 + 0.060): each H743 at 400 mA, the maximum at TJ 85 C at 400 MHz with all
       peripherals enabled (PRINTED, ST DS12110 Rev 10 Table 30 p.111; rv-pwr's HIGH) plus 60 mA of its other parts (DECLARED); by the case's
       method, constant power, 7.0380 W: 1.4358 A at U7's 4.9019 V (what leaves U7) and 1.4749 A at U601's own least load voltage 4.7719 V (MODEL,
       a bound: an LDO draws its output current, not constant power); the largest against U601's 3 A rating (PRINTED, SLUSEA4D): HOLDS
       LABELLED SCENARIO, not the case (Table 30's last column, TJ 125 C: 840 mA): 2.70 A of LDO current, under U601's 3 A, but 900 mA an LDO
       against the AP2112K's 600 mA (PRINTED IOUT(MAX) minimum): the LDO bounds it first, with or without this draft (finding L9T5-F06)
   (3) U601's limit against J_5V_IOC's VH 10 A (PRINTED, with AWG 16 on the standard header): high-side limit 4.2 / 5.0 / 5.8 A, low-side
       2.9 / 3.8 / 4.5 A (PRINTED); the output at most about (5.8 + 4.5) / 2 = 5.15 A (Equation 11, approximate, on PRINTED maxima), hiccup
       on a sustained short (9.3.12): HOLDS
   (4) L601 XAL6060-682ME: Isat 9.2 A (TYPICAL: Coilcraft's table, the current for a 30 % inductance drop, typical, at 25 C) over the part's
       5.8 A highest high-side limit (PRINTED): HOLDS (round 2 labelled the Isat PRINTED; it is a typical figure)
   (5) +5V_IOC's set point: 56.2k over 10.7k at 0.1 % and 25 ppm/K over 65 K (DECLARED, stream s99a's pair, as U41), VFB 0.784 to 0.816 V over TJ
       -40 to 150 C and IFB 0.15 uA either way (PRINTED, its sign not printed): 5.002 V nominal, 4.8719 to 5.1329 V; under the AP2112K's 6.0 V input
       maximum (PRINTED): HOLDS (the LDOs' least input is board B's item B3)
   (6) RAIL_EN with U601's EN on it (R2 100k over R184 39k, DECLARED; the TPS62933's EN pull-up Ip 0.7 uA and Ih 1.4 uA, TYPICAL only, no limit
       printed; 3 TPS62933 EN pins on the net, U12, U41 and U601): 2.983 V at 10 V, 4.890 V at 16.8 V, 5.227 V at the SMCJ18A's 18 V standoff; U601
       adds 0.0589 V; against VEN_RISE 1.28 V maximum and EN's 5.5 V recommended (6 V absolute) maximum (PRINTED): HOLDS
   (7) the enable RELATION (netlist, section 4 EN): U7's EN (DEV_EN) is pulled to +3V3 by R42 and driven by U27; +3V3 is U12's output, enabled
       by RAIL_EN; U601's EN is on RAIL_EN. So U601 is ENABLED whenever U7 can be enabled. That is connectivity, not timing: it does NOT show
       that +5V_IOC is in regulation whenever +5V_DEV is (round 3 said 'the supervisors are up whenever the device rail is': WITHDRAWN as
